WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.240
Hey everyone, привет, welcome to привет русский эпизод 38

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:08.040
for 12 июня 2026 года.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:12.320
I am allia, and today we are going to learn some really fun Russian words.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:12.840
Ready?

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:13.760
Поехали.

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:15.400
That means let's go.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:17.960
Our word of the day is Солнце.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:18.920
Солнце.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.680
It sounds like солнце.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:24.500
Picture a beat yellow soul like solar shining down.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.640
Солнце is your sonny shortcut.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.640
Today the sun is shining.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:30.900
Сегодня светит солнце.

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:32.080
Repeat after me.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:33.020
Солнце.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.840
Now let's build more weather words.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.220
The next word is дождь.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:39.060
Дождь.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:40.980
It sounds like дождь.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:43.120
Дождь means rain.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:44.500
It is raining.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:45.920
Идет дождь.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:46.900
Repeat after me.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:47.800
Дождь.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.740
The Russian word дождь and the English word

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.560
drizzle share an ancient route.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.420
This route meant to drip.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:57.000
The word traveled through all languages

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.820
and became dождь in Russian.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.100
Be careful though.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.240
Дождь sounds a bit like drenched.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:04.260
Yet it simply means rain.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:06.380
Next time you see drizzle,

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.940
remember it is cousins with dождь.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.340
They both come from the same dripping root.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.880
That connection is your secret shortcut

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:15.100
to remembering it forever.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:18.100
Next comes снег, снег.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:19.900
It sounds like снег.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:21.380
снег means snow.

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:23.280
In winter snow falls.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:24.860
Zimoi падает снег.

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:26.180
Repeat after me.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:27.080
снег.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:29.040
Now we add ветер.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:29.940
ветер.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:31.900
It sounds like вайтер.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:33.060
ветер means wind.

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:33.900
Strong wind.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:35.060
сильный ветер.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:36.000
Repeat after me.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:36.920
ветер.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.240
The next word is облака.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:40.140
Облака.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:42.460
It sounds like об лака.

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:44.320
Облака means cloud.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:46.500
There is a cloud in the sky.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:47.940
В небе облака.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:49.580
Repeat after me.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:50.380
Облака.

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.740
Let's learn тепло.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:53.740
тепло.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:55.840
It sounds like te-plow.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:57.380
тепло means warm.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:58.860
Today it is warm.

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:00.220
Сегодня тепло.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:01.320
Repeat after me.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:02.160
тепло.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.520
Next is холодно.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:05.740
холодно.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:07.980
It sounds like ho-lodna.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.000
холодно means cold.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:11.520
It is cold outside.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:13.280
На улице холодно.

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:14.380
Repeat after me.

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:15.200
холодно.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:17.000
Now we have graza.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:17.780
Graza.

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:19.580
It sounds like graza.

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:21.400
Graza means thunderstorm.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:22.840
Loud thunderstorm.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:23.960
Gromkaya graza.

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:25.060
Repeat after me.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:25.640
Graza.

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:27.820
Finaly comes raduga.

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:28.660
Raduga.

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:30.520
It sounds like raduga.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:32.600
Raduga means rainbow.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:34.520
After the rain rainbow.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:36.080
После дождя raduga.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:37.060
Repeat after me.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:37.840
Raduga.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.340
Let's look at a simple grammar idea.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:43.440
Russian weather phrases often used the word есть.

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:44.420
For there is.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:47.000
You can also just say the word alone.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.340
Есть дождь means there is rain.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:51.240
холодно means it is cold.

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:54.800
Unlike English, you do not always need it is.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.660
The word stands by itself.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.100
Now you can say a full weather sentence.

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:01.440
Russians love talking about the weather.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.420
Winters are long and cold.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:06.920
People often ask как пагода, when they greet friends.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.420
Sunny days bring picnics in the park.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:11.460
Time for our practice challenge.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:13.820
Do you remember what солнце means?

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:16.900
Try using one new word in a sentence today.

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:20.620
For kids, draw a sun and say солнце three times.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:24.000
For adults, look out the window and describe the weather.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:27.460
Now here is something really cool about one of today's words.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.620
Want to know a secret about дождь?

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:35.000
Did you know that дождь and the English word drizzle share an ancient route?

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:36.920
This route meant to drip.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:40.800
The word travelled through old languages and became dождь in Russian.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.080
Be careful though.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:44.120
Dождь sounds a bit like drenched.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:45.940
Yet it simply means rain.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:49.960
Next time you see drizzle, remember it is cousins with dождь.

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:52.540
They both come from the same dripping route.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:56.240
That connection is your secret shortcut to remembering it forever.

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:58.440
And that's our lesson for today.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.580
Молодец, for sticking with it.

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:04.800
Try using today's words in one real sentence before the next episode.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:07.700
Little steps, big progress, пока friends.

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:08.920
That's bye.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:10.980
And if you'd rather watch them, listen.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.880
Find us on YouTube at NerraRU.

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:15.420
Links in the show notes.

